# Baseline .dockerignore — copied/merged into a project by `dockerignore-init`.
# The whole build context is sent to the daemon and `COPY . .` bakes it into a
# layer that outlives any later `rm`, so secrets come first. Pass credentials a
# build needs with `--secret` instead of shipping the file.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a bare pattern here matches only at the context root:
# `node_modules` misses `web/node_modules`. Hence the `**/` prefixes.

# --- secrets and credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.sample
!**/.env.template
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/.npmrc
**/.yarnrc.yml
**/.pypirc
**/.netrc
**/.ssh
**/.gnupg
**/.aws
**/.azure
**/.kube
**/.docker
**/credentials.json
**/service-account*.json
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/.terraform
**/.private

# --- version control
.git
.hg
.svn

# --- dependencies and caches (reinstall inside the image)
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/bower_components
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.tox
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.gradle
**/.next
**/.nuxt
**/.turbo
**/coverage

# --- editor and OS junk
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.log
